@{b}Licence@{ub}

RadeonGL (c) 2026 Marcus Gerards. The full text is Licences/RadeonGL.txt
in the RadeonGL drawer; in short:

    * minigl.library contains MiniGL -- the library shell and the
      minigl.library 29.1 programming interface -- and is therefore under
      the Hyperion MiniGL Open Source License (Licences/MiniGL.txt): it may
      only be used on AmigaOS, and the source code of every change to it
      has to be published.
    * RadeonGL's complete source code is published at
      https://github.com/bubbob42/RadeonGL, and the package carries it
      in its Source drawer. Its own code is also available under the MIT
      licence.
    * The R200 microcode is (c) Advanced Micro Devices, MIT licence
      (Licences/R200-Microcode.txt). The register definitions follow the
      MIT-licensed Linux radeon, Mesa r200 and xf86-video-ati drivers;
      their notices are in Licences/RadeonGL.txt.

@{b}Made with AI@{ub}

RadeonGL was made with the help of AI. Claude, an AI model by Anthropic,
wrote most of its code, its tests and these manuals, working under the
direction of Marcus Gerards, who made the design decisions. Every release
was tested on real hardware.

