@node History "History"
@toc Main
@prev Licences

@{b}History@{ub}

0.9 (8.11.2026)
    * contexts in a window and in a bitmap: in the program's own window
      (mglCreateContextFromWindow), in a window RadeonGL opens on the
      default public screen (mglChooseWindowMode), or straight into the
      program's bitmap (mglCreateContextFromBitMap), on 15-, 16- and
      32-bit screens of the Radeon; resizable
    * several programs at once, each with its own context
    * lighting on the Radeon: glLight, glMaterial, glLightModel,
      glColorMaterial, glNormalPointer; eight lights, directional, local
      and spot, with attenuation and two-sided lighting
    * texture coordinate generation (glTexGen: object linear, eye
      linear, sphere map) and texture matrices
    * fog (glFog), wide lines (glLineWidth), glReadPixels and
      mglWriteShotPPM
    * textures with 8 bits a component for GL_RGBA8 and GL_RGB8
    * lit compiled vertex arrays take the fast path too
    * GLQuake as fast as with 0.8

0.8 (7.11.2026)
    * every screen mode of the card: Picasso96's own list stops at 256
      modes, and 1680 x 1050 to 1920 x 1440 were missing
    * programs switch the screen mode while they run
      (mglResizeContext), open a context in a chosen mode
      (mglCreateContextFromID), and hear why a mode was refused
      (GL_RGL_resize_error)
    * vertical sync (mglEnableSync): no tearing
    * no more columns of an old picture at 800 x 600, 1680 x 1050 and
      other widths that are not a multiple of 64 (the depth buffer in
      whole tiles)
    * a GL screen behind another screen is not drawn
    * the upload cache keeps working once full: GLQuake demo1 +3%
    * RadeonGLMove16 (MOVE16 bursts, off by default) and
      RadeonGLDisplayPriority
    * the Install icon is AmigaOS 3.2's installer icon by Martin "Mason"
      Merz

0.7 (6.11.2026)
    * the mouse pointer is hidden on the GL screen when a program asks
      (mglSetPointer)
    * the upload cache grows from 1 MB to 2 MB of card memory: less sent
      over the bus every frame
    * GL_RGL_static_arrays, RadeonGL's own extension: two hints for
      programs whose vertex arrays and index lists never change; GLQuake's
      RadeonGL edition draws its world from them
    * the card test tools also work on a 24-bit Workbench
    * tested with the Prometheus Firestorm PCI bridge too

0.6 (5.11.2026)
    * the Radeon finishes a frame while the processor builds the next:
      GLQuake demo1 at 1280 x 720 from 19.9 to 23.5 fps (RadeonGLOverlap)
    * the texture memory goes beside the program's own screen, whatever
      the Workbench's screen mode

0.5 (5.11.2026)
    * 16 MB of texture memory on an 8- or 16-bit Workbench too: 0.4 got
      8 MB there, and GLQuake showed white menu text and froze

0.4 (3.11.2026)
    * first release
    * GLQuake demo1 at 23.7 fps at 320 x 240 on a 68060/50 (command check
      off), 24.9 fps with RadeonGLDirect=1 and 8-bit lightmaps
    * a second build for a 68020 or 68030 with a 68881 or 68882
    * vertices sent again unchanged stay in the card's memory
    * one Picasso96 lock a frame
    * four demos: Spinner, Glow, Landscape, Showcase
@endnode
